export const modernPerspective = [
  'A plane-wave cutoff, a Brillouin-zone k-point mesh, and an FFT or charge-density grid are three different numerical resolutions. Increasing one does not automatically converge the others. A calculation can be tightly converged in its orbital basis and still be under-sampled in k space or under-resolved on a real-space grid.',
  'Plane waves provide a systematic basis, but the cutoff required for a target accuracy depends strongly on the chosen pseudopotential or PAW dataset. Cutoff convergence establishes representation convergence for that dataset; it does not establish pseudopotential transferability or the accuracy of the exchange–correlation approximation.',
